<title>USA: Georgia gets $20 mln PL480 purchase for wheat.</title>
<headline>Georgia gets $20 mln PL480 purchase for wheat.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department issued an authorization for Georgia to buy $20 million of U.S. wheat under Public Law 480, the agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The authorization provides for about 95,000 tonnes of wheat grade U.S. No. 2 or better, except that durum shall grade U.S. No. 3 or better, in bulk, the agency said.</p>
<p>The delivery period begins July 15 and ends on Dec. 31.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
</text>
